From 82231b3744019e43241534096b698bb87cb2fed6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: crazynucfan <127292955+crazynucfan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:31:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: negroni_defconfig: kernel BTF

Cilium's BPF masquerade program needs kernel BTF (without it the
verifier rejects tail_handle_snat_fwd_ipv4), and from Cilium 1.19.8 and
1.20.2 on so do its socket-LB programs. Build with full DWARF instead
of the reduced kind and generate BTF for the kernel and its modules
(/sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux), like Debian's own kernels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
index 71a3e1135..824bf1eaf 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/negroni_defconfig
@@ -1312,7 +1312,7 @@ CONFIG_IRQ_POLL=y
 CONFIG_PRINTK_TIME=y
 CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
 CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_DWARF_TOOLCHAIN_DEFAULT=y
-CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_REDUCED=y
+CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y
 CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ=y
 CONFIG_SCHEDSTATS=y
 # CONFIG_FTRACE is not set
-- 
2.43.0

